==============================================================================
1.  r_Q(R) IS UNBOUNDED (additive norm-R layer) -- closed-form check
==============================================================================
Square ZZ^2 (disc -4): r2(5^k) = 4(k+1) -> infinity
   R=5^0=1         r2=  4   (formula 4(k+1)=4)
   R=5^1=5         r2=  8   (formula 4(k+1)=8)
   R=5^2=25        r2= 12   (formula 4(k+1)=12)
   R=5^3=125       r2= 16   (formula 4(k+1)=16)
   R=5^4=625       r2= 20   (formula 4(k+1)=20)
   R=5^5=3125      r2= 24   (formula 4(k+1)=24)
   R=5^6=15625     r2= 28   (formula 4(k+1)=28)
Triangular ZZ[w] (disc -3): r(7^k) = 6(k+1) -> infinity
   R=7^0=1         r =  6   (formula 6(k+1)=6)
   R=7^1=7         r = 12   (formula 6(k+1)=12)
   R=7^2=49        r = 18   (formula 6(k+1)=18)
   R=7^3=343       r = 24   (formula 6(k+1)=24)
   R=7^4=2401      r = 30   (formula 6(k+1)=30)
=> BOTH 2D lattices have UNBOUNDED additive norm-R layers; kappa<=6 caps ONLY R=Rmin.

